{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DJBFQrmzTMd6eFgLPeFczP","type":"tool_result","content":"1170\t    {\n1171\t      \"id\": \"US-051\",\n1172\t      \"title\": \"Update generate_lesson skill — encourage inline markdown images + Image widget for key illustrations\",\n1173\t      \"description\": \"As an agent generating lessons, I want explicit guidance to use inline markdown images and the Image widget for key illustrations, so generated lessons are visually rich rather than wall-of-text.\",\n1174\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1175\t        \"scripts/ralph/skills/generate_lesson/SKILL.md updated with a new section 'Visual Illustrations' immediately after the Source Research section from US-041\",\n1176\t        \"Skill instructs: every theory section ≥300 chars long should include at least one inline markdown image `![alt](url)` where it makes pedagogical sense\",\n1177\t        \"Skill instructs: use the Image widget (US-050) as a standalone section for hero illustrations, diagrams, or figures that warrant their own caption + attribution treatment\",\n1178\t        \"Skill instructs: prefer Wikimedia Commons, public-domain repositories, official documentation diagrams (scikit-image, OpenCV, matplotlib), arxiv figure references; AVOID hotlinking from blog hosts likely to break (medium, towardsdatascience, personal blogs)\",\n1179\t        \"Skill instructs: every image (inline or widget) MUST have meaningful alt text describing what is shown — never empty alt, never 'image' placeholder\",\n1180\t        \"Skill instructs: provide attribution for Image widget when source mandates (Wikimedia → 'Wikimedia Commons, <author>, <license>')\",\n1181\t        \"Worked example in SKILL.md updated to include one inline markdown image (with Wikimedia URL) and one Image widget section\",\n1182\t        \"Typecheck passes\"\n1183\t      ],\n1184\t      \"priority\": 51,\n1185\t      \"passes\": false,\n1186\t      \"notes\": \"Skill-only changes (markdown + worked examples).\",\n1187\t      \"tags\": []\n1188\t    },\n1189\t    {\n1190\t      \"id\": \"US-052\",\n1191\t      \"title\": \"LessonChat — sliding side panel UI scaffold + persisted draft in localStorage\",\n1192\t      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want a sliding side panel inside lessons where I can compose questions to an AI tutor and have my draft preserved across page reloads, so I can come back to a question without retyping.\",\n1193\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1194\t        \"Right column of lesson view (US-015 chatCol) becomes a controlled panel: 0px when closed, 320px when open; transition 180ms; prefers-reduced-motion disables animation\",\n1195\t        \"Toggle: existing tutor button (⌘.) in lesson toolbar (currently disabled/grey from US-015) becomes active and toggles the panel; ⌘. keyboard shortcut (US-021) likewise toggles\",\n1196\t        \"Panel chrome: header with 'AI Tutor' title + close X button; scrollable body for message list; sticky footer with composer (textarea + Send button + Stop button placeholder)\",\n1197\t        \"Composer textarea autoresizes (max 6 lines); Enter inserts newline; ⌘+Enter (or Ctrl+Enter) triggers Send; Send button disabled when textarea empty or whitespace-only\",\n1198\t        \"Message list area shows placeholder copy when empty: 'Ask anything about this lesson — I have its content as context.' centered, --text-tertiary --fs-sm\",\n1199\t        \"Send (in this story) appends a user-message bubble to the message list and clears the textarea — no backend call yet (backend lands in US-053); a placeholder assistant bubble with 'Backend not connected — try again after US-053 ships' is appended for visibility during dev\",\n1200\t        \"Draft persistence: textarea value mirrored to `localStorage['lessonChatDraft:<courseSlug>:<lessonSlug>']` on each keystroke (debounced 200ms); restored on mount\",\n1201\t        \"Draft cleared from localStorage when message Send appends to