6,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":340},\"output_tokens\":42,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"951b4940-59c9-45a3-ba97-d8bc93a78325\",\"uuid\":\"c0d8d4cb-6bae-4c13-8f18-63bc3fe4fc8a\"}\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01HdSayGrzVs85BjSqd3ZeKk\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t# Ralph Progress Log\\n2\\tRotated: Sun May  3 20:56:44 CEST 2026\\n3\\tPrevious log archived to: archive/progress-2026-05-03-2056.txt\\n4\\t---\\n5\\t\\n6\\t## 2026-05-04 00:50 - US-049\\n7\\t- Implemented Video widget — embeds YouTube via `<iframe src='youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>?enablejsapi=1&rel=0&modestbranding=1[&start=N][&autoplay=1]'>` (16:9 responsive `aspect-ratio` container) or HTML5 `<video controls>` for MP4. Optional collapsible transcript panel below the player; click a segment to seek the player (postMessage `seekTo` for YouTube, `el.currentTime = N` for MP4). Active segment highlights in `--accent-subtle` driven by `timeupdate` (MP4) or YouTube iframe API `infoDelivery` events polled at 250 ms. Speaker labels rendered as small uppercase prefix per the AC styling. `extractYouTubeId()` accepts: bare 11-char id, `youtu.be/<id>`, `youtube.com/watch?v=<id>` (incl. `m.youtube.com` and `youtube-nocookie.com`), `/embed/<id>`, `/shorts/<id>`.\\n8\\t- Files added:\\n9\\t  - `src/widgets/Video/{schema.ts, sample.ts, VideoWidget.tsx, VideoEditor.tsx}`\\n10\\t  - `src/widgets/schemas/video.json` (regenerated by `npm run build:schemas`)\\n11\\t  - `courses/video-test/{course.json, lessons/neural-net-intro.json, lessons/mp4-demo.json}` — smoke-test course (YouTube + MP4 lessons)\\n12\\t- Files changed:\\n13\\t  - `src/widgets/registry.ts` — `video` entry (Video icon from lucide-react, `--widget-video` accent), `WidgetType` union extended\\n14\\t  - `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts` — added `video` to widget map\\n15\\t  - `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` — `VideoSectionSchema` variant added to discriminated union\\n16\\t  - `src/styles/tokens.css` — `--widget-video` CSS var in both light (`#b94a6f`) + dark (`#e08aa8`) blocks\\n17\\t  - `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx` — wired `VideoEditor` into `WidgetEditPanel`, added `video` body branch in `SectionRenderer`\\n18\\t  - `src/app/api/courses/[slug]/assets/[...path]/route.ts` — extended asset route's `CONTENT_TYPES` map with `.mp4 → video/mp4` and `.webm → video/webm` so course-hosted MP4 files served via the asset API have a correct Content-Type\\n19\\t  - `src/lib/schemas/schemas.test.ts` — discriminated-union case for `video` + dedicated `VideoData` schema tests + `extractYouTubeId` tests covering id-only, youtu.be, watch?v=, /embed/, /shorts/, mobile/nocookie hosts, and rejection of non-YouTube and bad input\\n20\\t  - `src/widgets/schemas/lesson.json` — regenerated\\n21\\t- Quality checks: `npm run typecheck` clean. `npm test` 7 files / 167 tests pass (added 12 new tests: 7 schema + 5 URL parser). `npm run lint` clean in `src/widgets/Video/` (only pre-existing errors remain in `claude/design/source/*.jsx` and `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/*.js`).\\n22\\t- Browser test (playwright headless on http://localhost:3049):\\n23\\t  - **YouTube** (`/tmp/playwright-test-us-049.js` → `/tmp/us-049-1-youtube.png`):\\n24\\t    - URL `watch?v=aircAruvnKk` rendered as `<iframe src='https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/aircAruvnKk?enablejsapi=1&rel=0&modestbranding=1'>`; `data-yt-id=\\\"aircAruvnKk\\\"` confirms parser extracted the id from the URL.\\n25\\t    - 5 transcript segments rendered; segment 0 shows speaker label `Grant` followed by the text.\\n26\\t    - Clicked segment index 3 (tStart=32) → `data-active=\\\"true\\\"` flipped to that segment within 300 ms (verified via `[data-testid^=\\\"video-transcript-seg-\\\"]` query).\\n27\\t    - Clicked the toggle → `[data-testid=\\\"video-transcript-list\\\"]` removed; clicked again → re-rendered.\\n28\\t    - Note: cross-origin postMessage on `iframe.contentWindow` cannot be intercepted from the parent, so seek verification on YouTube is via observable side-effects (active flip, no JS error). The seek mechanism itself is exercised end-to-end on the MP4 path where currentTime IS observable.\\n29\\t  - **MP4** (`/tmp/playwright-test-us-049-mp4.js` → `/tmp/us-049-2-mp4.png`):\\n30\\t    - `/api/courses/video-test/assets/sample.mp4` 404s (no real asset committed) but the `<video>` element is still rendered with `controls`, `src`, `autoplay=false`. The 404 is expected and documented in the test.\\n31\\t    - `startAt: 5` → on mount `video.currentTime` reads `5` (verified BEFORE installing the descriptor override).\\n32\\t    - Installed a `currentTime` setter spy → clicked segment 1 (tStart=10) → spy captured `[10]`.\\n33\\t    - Speaker label `Narrator` appears on segment 1.\\n34\\t- **Assumptions made (no human in the loop):**\\n35\\t  - \\\"Embed via youtube-nocookie.com\\\" interpreted as the privacy-enhanced domain regardless of input host. Both `youtube.com/watch?v=...` and `youtu.be/...` URLs map to `youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>` for embedding.\\n36\\t  - YouTube iframe","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/nukeemann/.claude/projects/-home-nukeemann-projects-ai-lecturer--worktrees-US-051/a5179973-6d3e-41c1-821c-3b55ae720415/tool-results/bwbd4cqpi.txt","persistedOutputSize":475920}}
